### Bugs

#### Critical Severity

## Vote Fetching Missing User Filter
**File:** lib/data/repositories/vote.repository.ts
**Severity:** Critical
**Issue:** The new app's vote fetching uses `voteRepository.findByChatId(id, ctx)` which only filters by chatId, while the old app used `getVotesByChatIdAndUserId({ chatId, userId })` filtering by BOTH chatId AND userId. This is a security/data isolation issue.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/lib/db/queries.ts:156-160 - `where(and(eq(vote.chatId, chatId), eq(vote.userId, userId)))`
**New Code:** lib/data/repositories/vote.repository.ts:599-603 - `where(eq(vote.chatId, chatId))` - missing userId filter
**Impact:** The new implementation returns ALL votes for a chat, not just the current user's votes. This could expose other users' vote data if they voted on messages in the same chat. In a shared/public chat scenario, users would see votes from all participants, not just their own.
**Remediation:** Add userId filter to the vote query in voteRepository.findByChatId or use a different method that includes userId filtering. The page should call a method like `findByChatIdAndUserId(chatId, userId, ctx)` instead.

#### High Severity

## Chat Component Missing fetchWithErrorHandlers
**File:** features/chat/components/chat.tsx
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The new Chat component uses the default fetch instead of the custom fetchWithErrorHandlers that handles authentication errors and session expiry.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/components/chat.tsx:200-202 - `fetch: fetchWithErrorHandlers` in transport config
**New Code:** features/chat/components/chat.tsx:132-144 - No custom fetch, uses default
**Impact:** Authentication errors and session expiry won't be handled properly. Users with expired sessions won't be redirected to login, instead they'll see generic errors or the app will behave unexpectedly.
**Remediation:** Import and use fetchWithErrorHandlers from lib/utils or lib/api for proper error handling.

## Chat Component Missing Data Stream Handlers
**File:** features/chat/components/chat.tsx
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The new Chat component's onData handler only handles "data-usage" type, missing handlers for artifact streaming, title updates, and message appending.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/components/chat.tsx:216-251 - Handles multiple data types:
  - data-usage (line 220-222)
  - data-chat-title with updateOptimisticChatTitle (line 223-226)
  - data-appendMessage with JSON parsing and validation (line 227-250)
  - Artifact streaming via setDataStream (line 217-219)
**New Code:** features/chat/components/chat.tsx:146-152 - Only handles data-usage:
  ```tsx
  onData: (dataPart) => {
      if (dataPart.type === "data-usage") {
          setUsage(dataPart.data as AppUsage)
      }
  },
  ```
**Impact:** Artifacts won't stream in real-time, chat titles won't update optimistically, and dynamically appended messages (like from tools) won't appear. The streaming experience is significantly degraded.
**Remediation:** Add all data type handlers from the old app, including artifact streaming, title updates, and message appending.

## Messages Component Missing useDataStream Hook
**File:** features/chat/components/messages.tsx
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The new Messages component doesn't call useDataStream() hook which is required for artifact streaming to work.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/components/messages.tsx:46 - `useDataStream();` called at component start
**New Code:** features/chat/components/messages.tsx - No useDataStream import or call
**Impact:** Artifact streaming won't work. The data stream context won't be consumed, so real-time artifact updates during AI response streaming won't be displayed.
**Remediation:** Import and call useDataStream hook from the data-stream-provider.

## Messages Component Missing useSettingsSnapshot for Auto-Scroll
**File:** features/chat/components/messages.tsx
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The new Messages component doesn't check the autoScroll setting from user preferences before auto-scrolling.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/components/messages.tsx:47,57-66 - Uses `const { autoScroll } = useSettingsSnapshot();` and checks it before scrolling:
  ```tsx
  useEffect(() => {
      if (status === "submitted" && autoScroll) {
          requestAnimationFrame(() => {
              virtuosoRef.current?.scrollToIndex({ ... });
          });
      }
  }, [status, autoScroll]);
  ```
**New Code:** features/chat/components/messages.tsx:89-94 - Always auto-scrolls without checking preference:
  ```tsx
  useEffect(() => {
      if (status === "submitted") {
          messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth" });
      }
  }, [status]);
  ```
**Impact:** Users who have disabled auto-scroll in settings will still have the view scrolled automatically. This ignores user preferences and can be disruptive for users who prefer manual scroll control.
**Remediation:** Import useSettingsSnapshot and check the autoScroll setting before auto-scrolling.

## Message Component Missing Tool Implementations
**File:** features/chat/components/message.tsx
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The new Message component has placeholder implementations for all tool invocations instead of the full implementations from the old app.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/components/message.tsx:188-311 - Full tool implementations:
  - tool-getWeather with Weather component (line 188-216)
  - tool-createDocument with DocumentPreview and error handling (line 218-240)
  - tool-updateDocument with DocumentPreview (line 242-269)
  - tool-requestSuggestions with DocumentToolResult (line 271-311)
**New Code:** features/chat/components/message.tsx:248-263 - Generic placeholder:
  ```tsx
  if (type.startsWith("tool-")) {
      return (
          <div key={key} className="...">
              <div className="font-medium">Tool: {type}</div>
              <div className="...">Tool result placeholder</div>
          </div>
      );
  }
  ```
**Impact:** Weather display, document creation/updates, and suggestion requests won't render properly. Users will see generic "Tool result placeholder" instead of actual tool outputs like weather cards or document previews.
**Remediation:** Implement all tool invocation UIs with their respective components (Weather, DocumentPreview, DocumentToolResult).

## Missing ChevronUp Icon in Dropdown Trigger
