### Functional Discrepancies

#### Critical Severity

## Missing Analytics Components
**File:** app/layout.tsx
**Severity:** Critical
**Issue:** Missing Vercel Analytics and Speed Insights components that were present in the old application
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/layout.tsx:76-77 - `<SpeedInsights />` and `<Analytics />` components
**New Code:** app/layout.tsx - These components are completely missing
**Impact:** Production monitoring and performance insights will not function. Vercel deployment will lack analytics data collection.
**Remediation:** Add imports for `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next` and `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`, then include both components in the body element.

#### High Severity

## Missing head.tsx with Resource Hints
**File:** app/layout.tsx (missing head.tsx)
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The old application had a dedicated head.tsx file with preconnect and dns-prefetch links for performance optimization. The new application has no equivalent.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/head.tsx:1-47 - Contains preconnect/dns-prefetch for:
  - cdn.jsdelivr.net (Pyodide CDN)
  - va.vercel-scripts.com (Vercel Analytics)
  - vitals.vercel-insights.com (Vercel Speed Insights)
  - fonts.gstatic.com (Google Fonts)
  - api.openai.com (OpenAI API)
  - generativelanguage.googleapis.com (Google AI)
  - api.open-meteo.com (Weather API)
**New Code:** No head.tsx exists; no preconnect/dns-prefetch links found in app/ directory
**Impact:** Performance degradation due to missing early DNS resolution and connection establishment for critical external resources. Slower font loading, API calls, and CDN access.
**Remediation:** Either create app/head.tsx with the same preconnect/dns-prefetch links, or integrate them into layout.tsx using Next.js metadata API or direct head elements.

## Missing Email Confirmation Flow in Register
**File:** features/auth/actions/register.action.ts
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The old app handled Supabase email confirmation flow - when email confirmation is enabled, Supabase returns a user but no session, and the app redirected to /login with a success message. The new app uses NextAuth with credentials provider and immediately signs in the user after creation, bypassing any email verification flow.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/(auth)/register/page.tsx:48-60 - Checks for `!data.session` after signup, shows toast "Account created! Please check your email to verify your account.", and redirects to /login
**New Code:** features/auth/actions/register.action.ts:60-77 - Immediately calls signIn() after createUser(), no email verification handling
**Impact:** If email verification is required by the authentication provider, users will be signed in without verifying their email. This bypasses email verification security measures. Additionally, the success message differs - old app showed specific email verification message, new app shows generic success.
**Remediation:** Implement email verification flow: after createUser(), check if email verification is required and handle accordingly (redirect to a "check your email" page instead of signing in immediately).

## Different Post-Login Redirect Path
**File:** features/auth/actions/login.action.ts
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The old app redirected to "/" after successful login, while the new app redirects to "/chat". This is a functional change in user flow.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx:92 - `router.push("/")`
**New Code:** features/auth/actions/login.action.ts:63 - `redirectTo: "/chat"`
**Impact:** Users will land on a different page after login. While this may be intentional (chat is the main feature), it changes the expected user flow. The old app's "/" route likely redirected to "/chat" anyway, but the direct path should be verified.
**Remediation:** Verify if "/" redirects to "/chat" in the old app. If so, this is an acceptable change. Otherwise, ensure the redirect target matches user expectations.

## Different Post-Registration Redirect Path
**File:** features/auth/actions/register.action.ts
**Severity:** High
**Issue:** The old app redirected to "/" after successful registration (with session), while the new app redirects to "/chat". Additionally, old app redirected to "/login" when email confirmation was needed.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/(auth)/register/page.tsx:58,111 - `router.push("/login")` for email confirmation, `router.push("/")` for immediate login
**New Code:** features/auth/actions/register.action.ts:76 - `redirectTo: "/chat"`
**Impact:** Same as login redirect issue - users land on different page. Also, the email confirmation redirect to /login is completely missing.
**Remediation:** Align redirect paths with old app behavior or document the intentional change.

## Missing Pyodide Script for Python Code Execution
**File:** app/(chat)/layout.tsx
**Severity:** High
