**Remediation:** Evaluate if AppSidebar needs SSR disabled. If it uses browser APIs (localStorage, window), wrap it in a dynamic import or use client-side guards.

## Chat Service Ownership Check Differs from Old App
**File:** lib/data/services/chat.service.ts
**Severity:** Medium
**Issue:** The new chatService.getWithMessages throws ForbiddenError for non-owners, while the old chatData.getWithMessages returned null. The page handles this differently.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/lib/data/chat.ts:275-278 - Returns null if chat not found or user doesn't own it
**New Code:** lib/data/services/chat.service.ts:125-133 - Throws ForbiddenError if userId doesn't match
**Impact:** The new implementation throws an exception for unauthorized access, which is caught by the try/catch and redirects with a generic "chat_not_found" notice. The old implementation returned null silently. Both end up at the same redirect, but the error logging is different. The new approach logs "chat_page_load_failed" instead of "chat_access_denied" for permission issues.
**Remediation:** Consider having the service return null for forbidden access (like the old app) or handle ForbiddenError separately in the page to log the correct error type.

## Error Handling Changed from Toast to Inline
**File:** app/(auth)/login/page.tsx, app/(auth)/register/page.tsx
**Severity:** Medium
**Issue:** The old app used toast notifications (toast() from @/components/toast) for all error and success messages. The new app displays errors inline below the form using local state. This changes the UX pattern for error feedback.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx:25-29,42-46 - Uses `toast({ type: "error", description: "..." })` for errors
**New Code:** app/(auth)/login/page.tsx:77-81 - Uses `{error && <p className="...">{error}</p>}` for inline error display
**Impact:** UX consistency change. Toast notifications appear at the top/bottom of the screen and auto-dismiss, while inline errors are persistent and positioned within the form. Users may miss inline errors more easily. Success messages are also missing in the new app (no toast on successful registration/login).
**Remediation:** Consider adding toast notifications back for consistency with the old app, or document this as an intentional UX change. Add success toasts for registration completion.

## Missing defaultEmail Prop Usage in Login Page
**File:** app/(auth)/login/page.tsx
**Severity:** Medium
**Issue:** The old login page preserved the submitted email in state and passed it to AuthForm as `defaultEmail`, so if the form re-rendered (e.g., after failed login), the email field would retain the user's input. The new app doesn't use this feature.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx:13,32,107 - `const [email, setEmail] = useState("")`, `setEmail(submittedEmail)`, `<AuthForm ... defaultEmail={email}>`
**New Code:** app/(auth)/login/page.tsx - No email state preservation; AuthForm receives no defaultEmail prop
**Impact:** Minor UX degradation - if login fails, the user has to re-type their email address. The old app preserved the email to reduce friction on failed login attempts.
**Remediation:** Add email state preservation in the login page, or rely on browser autofill (which may work if autocomplete="email" is set correctly).

## Auth Layout Redirects Authenticated Users
**File:** app/(auth)/layout.tsx
**Severity:** Medium
**Issue:** The new auth layout checks if user is authenticated and redirects to /chat. The old app didn't have this protection in the layout - each auth page was self-contained with its own layout wrapper.
**Old Code:** archive/oldapp/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx:97-98 - No authenticated user redirect; full page layout inline
**New Code:** app/(auth)/layout.tsx:36-42 - `if (session?.user) { redirect("/chat") }`
